[bug · low] Value-normalization break for legacy cursors: pre-deploy cursors always encoded the
`scene_code` key, with value `None` when no scene filter was set (the common case). The new check
computes `requested = scene_code or ""` and compares `ctx.get(field) != requested`, so `None != ""`
rejects an in-flight legacy cursor with 422 during a rolling upgrade — contradicting the comment
above that claims legacy cursors still validate under the old view/scene_code semantics. Suggest
normalizing both sides, e.g. `(ctx.get(field) or "") != requested`.

